---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

// The interop demo needs ISOLATED documents: on this page the framework's
// layers are already declared, so a page-level @layer app-reset {} would be
// declared later and outrank them — the exact ordering trap the recipe
// exists to teach. Each iframe implements the full recipe from scratch.
const cssHref = base + '/assets/busy-office-ui.min.css';
const hostileReset = 'button { background: transparent; border: 0; padding: 0; font: inherit; color: inherit; }';
const iframeRaw = `<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="${cssHref}">
<style>/* Tailwind-v3-preflight-style reset, UNLAYERED — beats every layer */
${hostileReset}</style>
<body style="margin:1rem"><button class="bo-btn">Approve order</button>`;
const iframeRecipe = `<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
@layer app-reset, bo-reset, bo-tokens, bo-primitives, bo-components, bo-utilities;
@import url("${cssHref}");
@layer app-reset { /* same reset, wrapped — now ranked below the framework */
${hostileReset} }
</style>
<body style="margin:1rem"><button class="bo-btn">Approve order</button>`;
const recipe = `/* app.css — the ONE statement that matters comes first: it fixes the
   layer order with your reset's layer ranked BELOW the framework's. */
@layer app-reset, bo-reset, bo-tokens, bo-primitives, bo-components, bo-utilities;
@import url("tailwind-or-normalize-or-reboot.css") layer(app-reset);
@import url("busy-office-ui.min.css");   /* or the npm import */

/* Your own overrides: write them UNLAYERED, as usual — unlayered still
   beats everything, which is the framework's normal override story. */`;
---
<Gallery title="Troubleshooting">
  <p class="demo-note">
    This framework's failure modes are unusually <em>silent</em> — modern CSS
    degrades by doing nothing, not by erroring. Symptom → cause:
  </p>
  <section class="demo">
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Symptom</th><th scope="col">Cause &amp; fix</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Dialogs / tabs / dropdowns do nothing</td><td>The behavior init was never called. <code>initDialogs()</code>, <code>initTabs()</code>, <code>initDropdowns()</code> — once each, anywhere, any time. See <a href={base + '/concepts/js-behaviors'}>JS behaviors</a>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Components render unstyled or half-styled à la carte</td><td>Import order: <strong>tokens, then reset, then components</strong>. Components carry only their own layer.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Your overrides don't apply</td><td>They're inside an <code>@layer</code>. Write app CSS <em>unlayered</em> — unlayered always wins. Never <code>!important</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Form error messages never appear</td><td>Below the browser floor (<code>:has()</code>/<code>:user-invalid</code>), interactive reveals are fail-closed. Server-set <code>aria-invalid</code> + message-as-sibling still works. Floor: Chrome/Edge 119 · FF 128 · Safari 17.4.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bulk-actions bar stale after an HTMX row swap</td><td>Only <code>htmx:afterSwap</code> re-derives automatically. Other swap mechanisms: call <code>refreshDataTable(container)</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Everything is 40% too small</td><td>The host page sets <code>html {'{'} font-size: 62.5% {'}'}</code>. The framework assumes an unmodified root — embed via iframe.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Density attribute seems ignored on one table</td><td>It's on a wrapper while the table sits in a narrow container — explicit density wins only when set on the table or its container element itself.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sort arrows render but clicking does nothing</td><td>By contract: your code re-orders rows and sets <code>aria-sort</code>; the CSS only draws the indicator.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Toast appears behind an open dialog</td><td>The dialog owns the browser top layer; z-index can't beat it. Render confirmations inside the dialog.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Checked rows POST nothing</td><td>Row checkboxes need <code>name</code>/<code>value</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Buttons/tables go unstyled the moment Tailwind (or an old reset) is added</td><td>The reset is <em>unlayered</em>, and unlayered CSS beats every <code>@layer</code> — by design. Wrap it: see below.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Using with Tailwind or an existing reset</h2>
    <p>All framework CSS lives in <code>@layer</code>, and your unlayered CSS
    always wins — that's the <a href={base + '/concepts/cascade'}>override
    story</a>. The flip side: an unlayered <em>reset</em> you didn't write
    (Tailwind v3 preflight, normalize.css, Bootstrap reboot, a CSS-in-JS
    global) also wins, and silently strips components — preflight's
    <code>button {'{'} background: transparent {'}'}</code> is the classic.
    Wrap the reset in a layer that ranks below the framework's:</p>
    <pre><code>{recipe}</code></pre>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">The order statement must be the <strong>first
    rule</strong> of the entry stylesheet — a layer's rank is fixed by where
    it first appears, so declaring <code>app-reset</code> before the
    framework's layers is what pins it underneath. Tailwind <strong>v4</strong>
    declares its own layers and coexists without wrapping; on v3 you can also
    just disable preflight (<code>corePlugins: {'{'} preflight: false {'}'}</code>).</p>
    <h3>Proof, live</h3>
    <div class="bo-cluster" style="align-items: stretch; --bo-cluster-gap: var(--bo-space-4)">
      <figure style="margin: 0">
        <iframe srcdoc={iframeRaw} title="Unlayered reset — button stripped" style="border: 1px solid var(--bo-color-border-default); border-radius: var(--bo-radius-md); inline-size: 16rem; block-size: 5rem; background: white"></iframe>
        <figcaption class="bo-u-text-muted" style="font-size: var(--bo-font-size-xs)">Reset unlayered: the button is stripped bare.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure style="margin: 0">
        <iframe srcdoc={iframeRecipe} title="Reset wrapped in a layer — button intact" style="border: 1px solid var(--bo-color-border-default); border-radius: var(--bo-radius-md); inline-size: 16rem; block-size: 5rem; background: white"></iframe>
        <figcaption class="bo-u-text-muted" style="font-size: var(--bo-font-size-xs)">Same reset wrapped in <code>app-reset</code>: framework wins.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Each frame is an isolated document running the
    exact same hostile reset — the only difference is the one
    <code>@layer</code> statement. (Frames pin a white background: they don't
    inherit the docs theme.)</p>
  </section>
</Gallery>
